WEBVTT

asr-000001
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:16.560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And my thanks to our civil society partners, support staff, and all participants who continue to engage in this process.

asr-000002
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:26.640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: This initiative began with House Resolution No. 94 and was operationalized through interim guidelines in 2025.

asr-000003
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:39.100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Today, it is sustained and strengthened by the reconstitution of the House Task Force on People's Participation.

asr-000004
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:51.200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: We know from global experience that meaningful civil society participation in budgeting improves targeting of public expenditures,

asr-000005
00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: strengthens accountability, and enhances surveillance.

asr-000006
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:09.640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Brazil's participatory budgeting showed how local involvement led to better health and sanitation outcomes,

asr-000007
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:18.900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: while Kenya's experience demonstrated how citizens' monitoring improved transparency and value for money.

asr-000008
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.180
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The Philippines has made important strides.

asr-000009
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yet, as the 2025 Open Budgeting,

asr-000010
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:38.940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: survey reminds us, our participation score of 37, though in ASEAN, remains below the level considered adequate.

asr-000011
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:51.860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: We must therefore expand opportunities for engagement, ensure inclusivity, and make participation more impactful across the budget cycle.

asr-000012
00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:56.620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: That is why I enjoin all CSOs here today,

asr-000013
00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:04.560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: to actively participate and remain vigilant throughout the budget process at all three levels.

asr-000014
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:13.820
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: First, agency level, shaping programs and allocations through budget partnership agreements.

asr-000015
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:26.100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Local level, which is the second, ensuring projects rise from barangay, demand-driven, plans through mandatory, bottom-up,

asr-000016
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.060
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: budgeting.

asr-000018
00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:54.720
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Third, audit level, monitoring how funds are spent and implemented through the citizens' participatory audit. Together, these three pillars from the foundation of a participatory budget system. With your vigilance, we can ensure that participation is not just a practice, but a right guaranteed by law under the proposed Philippine

asr-000019
00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Budgeting Code.

asr-000020
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Hopefully, madiscuss din po natin ito mamaya.

asr-000021
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:09.120
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And may this process continue to deepen the partnership between Congress and the people.

asr-000022
00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:26.480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Together, we can work forward, work towards a national budget that is transparent, participatory, and truly responsive to the needs and aspiration of every

asr-000023
00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.720
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Filipino.

asr-000024
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.000
