02:44:45.800 --> 02:44:46.910
John Castillo: Thank you very much,

asr-003829
02:44:46.910 --> 02:44:48.910
John Castillo: Vice Chair Arnie Fuentebella.

asr-003830
02:44:48.910 --> 02:44:50.910
John Castillo: And we, just

asr-003831
02:44:50.910 --> 02:44:52.910
John Castillo: like that, we have reached our

asr-003832
02:44:52.910 --> 02:44:54.910
John Castillo: final segment of

asr-003833
02:44:54.910 --> 02:44:56.910
John Castillo: today's People's Budget Review.

asr-003834
02:44:56.910 --> 02:44:58.910
John Castillo: But to give his

asr-003835
02:44:58.910 --> 02:45:00.910
John Castillo: closing remarks.

asr-003836
02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:06.980
John Castillo: may we call on the Deputy Secretary-General of the Congressional Policy and Budget Research Department,

asr-003837
02:45:08.040 --> 02:45:11.140
John Castillo: Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral.

asr-003838
02:45:11.680 --> 02:45:16.320
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Good afternoon to all of us.

asr-003839
02:45:16.780 --> 02:45:21.940
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: First of all, we would like to express our deepest appreciation and gratitude

asr-003840
02:45:21.940 --> 02:45:28.440
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: to our legislators present here, led by Senior Vice Chair Garcia

asr-003841
02:45:28.440 --> 02:45:33.800
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and the other vice chairpersons of the Committee on Appropriation,

asr-003842
02:45:33.800 --> 02:45:41.260
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Congresswoman Garcia, Congressman Arrogancia, Congresswoman Lagdameo,

asr-003843
02:45:42.160 --> 02:45:49.660
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Congressman Fuentebella, Congresswoman Bondoc, and Congresswoman Suansing.

asr-003844
02:45:49.860 --> 02:45:50.620
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Thank you so much.

asr-003845
02:45:50.780 --> 02:45:56.440
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: And to all our CSO representatives here present, again, marami pong salamat.

asr-003846
02:45:56.440 --> 02:45:58.440
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: As we conclude...

asr-003847
02:45:58.440 --> 02:46:04.620
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: As we conclude today's People's Budget Review, allow me to begin with a very familiar story.

asr-003848
02:46:05.500 --> 02:46:08.060
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: The story of the blind man and the elephant.

asr-003849
02:46:09.000 --> 02:46:12.800
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Each man touched a different part of the elephant.

asr-003850
02:46:13.580 --> 02:46:18.740
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: One touched the trunk and said the elephant was like a snake.

asr-003851
02:46:19.460 --> 02:46:22.760
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Another touched the leg and said it was like a tree.

asr-003852
02:46:23.300 --> 02:46:27.640
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Another touched the side and said it was like a wall.

asr-003853
02:46:28.440 --> 02:46:36.920
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: It was describing something real, but none, by himself, had the complete picture.

asr-003854
02:46:36.920 --> 02:46:41.720
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: In many ways, this is also true of the national budget.

asr-003855
02:46:41.720 --> 02:46:48.780
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Government agencies see it from the perspective of programs and implementation.

asr-003856
02:46:48.780 --> 02:46:55.620
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Economic managers see it from the perspective of fiscal discipline and national priorities.

asr-003857
02:46:55.620 --> 02:47:01.280
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Congress sees it through its constitutional power of the purse

asr-003866
02:47:01.280 --> 02:47:04.960
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and its responsibility to represent the people.

asr-003875
02:47:05.880 --> 02:47:09.180
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Researchers examine the numbers and evidence

asr-003882
02:47:09.380 --> 02:47:17.940
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and CSOs and people's organizations see how government policies and programs are actually

asr-003883
02:47:17.940 --> 02:47:21.200
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: experienced by communities.

asr-003884
02:47:21.200 --> 02:47:28.660
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Each perspective is important, but no single perspective gives us the whole picture.

asr-003885
02:47:28.660 --> 02:47:34.020
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: This is why evidence-based budgeting is so important.

asr-003886
02:47:34.020 --> 02:47:40.440
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: When Congress decides how trillions of pesos of public resources should be allocated, we

asr-003887
02:47:40.440 --> 02:47:44.840
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: should be able to answer some very basic questions.

asr-003888
02:47:44.840 --> 02:47:48.820
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: What problems are we trying to solve?

asr-003889
02:47:48.820 --> 02:47:52.300
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: What has the government already spent on?

asr-003890
02:47:52.300 --> 02:47:54.800
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: What has the spending produced?

asr-003891
02:47:54.800 --> 02:47:57.000
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Is the program working?

asr-003892
02:47:57.000 --> 02:47:58.900
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Who has benefited?

asr-003893
02:47:58.900 --> 02:48:01.460
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: And what should we do differently?

asr-003894
02:48:01.460 --> 02:48:04.000
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Unfortunately, the evidence needed to

asr-003895
02:48:04.000 --> 02:48:11.460
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: answer these questions is often fragmented across agencies and information systems.

asr-003896
02:48:11.460 --> 02:48:17.980
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: We have financial information on how much has been obligated and disbursed, but information

asr-003897
02:48:17.980 --> 02:48:23.740
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: on what government actually delivered and what outcomes those expenditures produced

asr-003898
02:48:23.740 --> 02:48:30.160
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: is not always as readily available, timely, or comparable.

asr-003899
02:48:30.160 --> 02:48:35.000
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: This points to the need for a more systematic approach to evidence gathering

asr-003900
02:48:35.000 --> 02:48:39.100
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: through a unified national monitoring

asr-003901
02:48:39.140 --> 02:48:41.620
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and evaluation system.

asr-003902
02:48:41.620 --> 02:48:48.380
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Such a system should identify a core set of critical performance indicators that every

asr-003903
02:48:48.380 --> 02:48:54.640
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: government agency is required to regularly report and publish.

asr-003904
02:48:54.640 --> 02:49:01.420
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: These indicators should allow us to follow the entire results chain, from inputs and

asr-003905
02:49:01.420 --> 02:49:05.000
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: expenditures to activities and outputs

asr-003907
02:49:05.000 --> 02:49:09.380
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and ultimately to outcomes and impacts.

asr-003908
02:49:09.380 --> 02:49:17.380
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: And this information should not remain scattered among individual agencies or buried in periodic

asr-003909
02:49:17.380 --> 02:49:18.860
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: reports.

asr-003910
02:49:18.860 --> 02:49:27.520
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: We need an integrated data system that allows Congress, government decision makers, CSOs,

asr-003911
02:49:27.520 --> 02:49:32.660
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: researchers, and ultimately the public to have real-time or near-real-time

asr-003912
02:49:32.780 --> 02:49:39.780
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: access to financial and performance information, especially given this age of

asr-003913
02:49:39.780 --> 02:49:42.380
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: information technology.

asr-003914
02:49:42.380 --> 02:49:47.560
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Imagine how this change could change budget deliberation.

asr-003915
02:49:47.560 --> 02:49:54.440
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Instead of asking how much did we appropriate or how much was spent, Congress could ask

asr-003916
02:49:54.440 --> 02:49:59.100
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: what did we accomplish and what we spent.

asr-003917
02:49:59.100 --> 02:50:03.340
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: This is the kind of evidence base we need for better budgeting.

asr-003918
02:50:03.340 --> 02:50:08.000
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: But even the best government information system cannot tell us everything.

asr-003919
02:50:08.000 --> 02:50:12.580
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Official indicators tell us what numbers show.

asr-003920
02:50:12.580 --> 02:50:17.980
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Citizens and civil society can help tell us what those numbers mean on the ground.

asr-003921
02:50:17.980 --> 02:50:23.480
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: This is where CSOs and people's organizations become indispensable.

asr-003922
02:50:23.500 --> 02:50:28.400
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: For legislators, civil society provides an important independent source of information

asr-003923
02:50:28.400 --> 02:50:31.000
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and evidence.

asr-003924
02:50:31.000 --> 02:50:38.020
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: CSOs can tell us whether services actually reach intended beneficiaries, whether a program

asr-003925
02:50:38.020 --> 02:50:45.040
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: that appears successful in an agency report is working in communities, and whether important

asr-003926
02:50:45.040 --> 02:50:47.520
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: needs have been overlooked.

asr-003927
02:50:47.520 --> 02:50:52.420
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: They help Congress see another part of the elephant.

asr-003928
02:50:52.420 --> 02:50:58.400
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: This is why the House of Representatives has taken steps to widen people's participation

asr-003929
02:50:58.400 --> 02:50:59.060
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: in the budget.

asr-003930
02:50:59.060 --> 02:51:08.080
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: We have established mechanisms for CSO accreditation and participation in agency budget hearings,

asr-003931
02:51:08.080 --> 02:51:14.140
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: provided opportunities for the submission of position papers and recommendations, undertaken

asr-003932
02:51:14.140 --> 02:51:21.840
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: budget literacy activities, expanded access to budget information, and created opportunities

asr-003933
02:51:21.840 --> 02:51:29.020
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: such as today's dialogue for civil society to engage directly with legislators.

asr-003934
02:51:29.060 --> 02:51:35.940
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: But we must also recognize that participation remains a work in progress.

asr-003935
02:51:35.940 --> 02:51:43.220
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Are we hearing from a sufficiently broad range of organizations, including those outside

asr-003936
02:51:43.220 --> 02:51:50.520
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Metro Manila and those representing marginalized communities? Do CSOs have the technical capacity

asr-003937
02:51:50.520 --> 02:51:53.940
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and information needed to participate effectively?

asr-003938
02:51:53.940 --> 02:51:59.060
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Are budget documents provided early enough and in forms that can be readily

asr-003939
02:51:59.060 --> 02:52:01.820
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: analyzed?

asr-003940
02:52:01.820 --> 02:52:07.540
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: And perhaps the most important question is whether participation actually influences

asr-003941
02:52:07.540 --> 02:52:08.540
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: decisions.

asr-003942
02:52:08.540 --> 02:52:17.300
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Moving forward, therefore, I believe we need to pursue two mutually reinforcing reforms.

asr-003943
02:52:17.300 --> 02:52:25.160
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: First, we need a stronger evidence infrastructure, a unified monitoring and evaluation system,

asr-003944
02:52:25.160 --> 02:52:28.360
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: common and critical performance indicators.

asr-003945
02:52:28.360 --> 02:52:35.680
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Interoperable information systems and real-time or near real-time access to financial and

asr-003946
02:52:35.680 --> 02:52:37.320
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: performance data.

asr-003947
02:52:37.320 --> 02:52:45.480
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Second, we need stronger participatory institutions, earlier engagements of CSOs, better access

asr-003948
02:52:45.480 --> 02:52:53.640
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: to information, stronger budget literacy, clearer channels between CSOs and legislators,

asr-003949
02:52:53.640 --> 02:52:59.940
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: and mechanisms for tracking how civil society recommendations are considered in the budget process.

asr-003952
02:53:01.380 --> 02:53:07.320
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Better data without participation can give us numbers without sufficient context.

asr-003953
02:53:08.800 --> 02:53:16.240
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Participation with good data can give us perspectives without sufficient evidence. We need both.

asr-003954
02:53:17.240 --> 02:53:20.700
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: And this brings us back to the blind man and the elephant.

asr-003955
02:53:20.700 --> 02:53:25.480
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: The objective is not merely to bring more people around the elephant.

asr-003959
02:53:26.000 --> 02:53:33.440
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: It is to ensure that it brings evidence from the part that he or she can see.

asr-003963
02:53:34.560 --> 02:53:41.820
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: And that's what we put all of that together to put the evidence into an understandable whole.

asr-003964
02:53:42.340 --> 02:53:48.600
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: That, I believe, is what a truly evidence-based and participatory budget process should accomplish.

asr-003965
02:53:48.940 --> 02:53:53.900
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Thus, on behalf of the Congressional Policy and Budget Research Department,

asr-003966
02:53:53.900 --> 02:54:03.180
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: I thank our members of Congress, our CSOs, PO partners, and everyone who participated in today's dialogue.

asr-003967
02:54:03.800 --> 02:54:08.900
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: May what we heard today find its way into our continuing budget deliberations,

asr-003968
02:54:10.020 --> 02:54:17.700
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: our oversight work, and our efforts to further institutionalize meaningful participation in Congress.

asr-003969
02:54:18.000 --> 02:54:23.880
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: Because ultimately, a people's budget should not only be a budget for the people,

asr-003970
02:54:23.900 --> 02:54:36.620
CPBRD Deputy Secretary General Dr. Romulo Emmanuel Miral Jr.: it should be a budget informed by evidence, accountable for results, and increasingly shaped with the people. Maraming salamat po at magandang hapon sa ating lahat.

asr-003971
02:54:40.860 --> 02:54:43.300
